{"action":"final","query":{"op":"none","id":null,"start":null,"end":null,"search":null,"groupBy":null},"diagnosis":"getLiveIntervals follows MemDescViewTrait users but stops at arith.select, so backing allocations can expire before loads through the selected descriptor. In case-24/25, the 64-column temporary overlaps both candidates and selected outputs become 7 (fact-24/26, fact-25). The 32-column temporary overlaps only the first candidate: case-27 fails while case-26 passes (fact-29/27, fact-28). Passing early-allocation controls place the temporary at column 64 (case-30/31, fact-33/35, fact-34). Case-32 also demonstrates legal reuse of the dead second allocation (fact-36/37). Extend the existing traversal through select results, transitively through mixed views and select chains; deduplicate visited operations to avoid repeated traversal of converging paths. Both possible backing allocations remain live through selected-result uses, while reuse after their last use remains available. First-fit allocation, alignment, row constraints, layout, and size rounding remain unchanged. Static IR and outputs support premature reuse but do not measure GPU write/read timestamps. The proposed repair has not been compiled or tested; no post-repair feedback is available.","locations":[{"source_id":"source-01","start_line":120,"end_line":135},{"source_id":"source-02","start_line":17,"end_line":26},{"source_id":"source-03","start_line":15,"end_line":24},{"source_id":"source-05","start_line":17,"end_line":26},{"source_id":"source-06","start_line":15,"end_line":21}],"evidence_ids":["case-24","case-25","fact-24","fact-26","fact-25","case-26","case-27","fact-27","fact-29","fact-28","case-30","case-31","fact-33","fact-35","fact-34","case-32","fact-36","fact-37","case-36","fact-42","fact-43"],"edits":[{"old":"  // Merge the alloc liverange with the liverange of any subview of the
